      "section": "Stem cells",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "A cross-section of a lily of the valley stem in two fluorescence channels, stored as one OME-TIFF file whose smaller levels are SubIFDs. The viewer fetches only the tiles it draws, with HTTP Range requests. Each point is a cell found between the walls; cells with bright Ch2 walls (the sheaths around the vascular bundles) are called thick-walled. Lasso cells to filter the table and the cards.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
